    "description": "3FTech PDW Sights: FFFTech/FFFTechnology\n\nA set of basic adjustable sights for carbines, PDWs, large pistols, etc. that fit onto a 1913 Picatinny rail. \nThe front sight is 3mm wide, and can be driven in/out for elevation adjustment. The rear sight is lateral drift \nadjustable, typical with pistol rear sights. A rear set screw secures the rear sight from being knocked out of \nposition, show the firearm it's mounted to be dropped. \n\nThree rear drift sights are available:\n\n *4mm U Notch\n *5mm U Notch\n *5.5mm Aperture\n\n\nPrinter Used: Monoprice Maker Select Plus\n\nFilament Used: PLA+\n\nPrint Settings:\n\nExtruder: 216C \nBed: 56C \nFirst Layer Print Height: .20mm \nStandard Layer Height: .14mm\nWall Thickness: .40mm\nWall Perimeters: 3 - 5\nInfill: 20%\nInfill Pattern: Gyroid\nMaterial Flow: 100%\nSupport Material Percentage: 16%\n\nPrint the front and rear sight mounts on their front faces, and the rear sight drift on it's rear, flattest face.\n\n\nHardware Needed: \n\n1x M5x30 Hex Socketed Machine Screw/Bolt\n\n1x M5 Hex Nut (Be sure both bolt & nut are the same thread pitch.)\n\n1x M3x10 Set Screw\n\n1x M3x5 Set Screw",
